=== ROOT-CAUSE PROBE (bounded, source grep at the pin, in-container) ===
- /opt/astra-sim/astra-sim/network_frontend/htsim/proto/HTSimProtoTcp.cc:102
  contains `srand(time(NULL));` — the frontend glue seeds the RNG from
  WALL-CLOCK TIME on every run.
- The compiled queues consume it: sim/compositequeue.cpp:72 and
  sim/aeolusqueue.cpp:81 use `if ((uint64_t)random() < p)` (drop decisions);
  sim/config.cpp:10 also calls rand().
- (The standalone csg-htsim datacenter/main_*.cpp entry points seed variously
  with fixed seeds or time; they are not in this binary's path.)
=> Mechanism: time-seeded RNG -> per-run packet-drop/RTO patterns -> different
   retransmission tails -> different straggler NPUs and Wall times. This is an
   upstream property of the integration at this pin, not a recipe error: same
   image, same binary hash, same inputs, two runs, two different (valid) outcomes.
   Implication for essun (hard rule 6, determinism): any future adapter must
   control seeding (e.g. LD_PRELOAD/time interception or an upstream seeding
   patch) before packet-level runs can be replay-verified. Recorded for S3.

